# AMCOS.Web.Core — example environment file.
#
# Copy to ".env" (same folder) to supply all app settings from one file instead of
# exporting each variable individually:
#     cp .env.example .env      (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# Program.cs loads this file on startup (KEY=VALUE lines; # comments allowed) and sets any
# variable that is not already defined in the environment. Nested config keys use the ASP.NET
# double-underscore convention (OpenIdConnect__ClientId  ->  OpenIdConnect:ClientId).
#
# IMPORTANT — Development vs. everything else:
#   * Development: you do NOT need this file. appsettings.Development.json already points at the
#     local Docker Keycloak (client "amcos-local") and Postgres. Running `dotnet run` in
#     Development and leaving these UNSET is the correct setup. Setting OpenIdConnect__* here (or
#     as stray shell variables) will OVERRIDE appsettings.Development.json and can cause the
#     Keycloak "Client not found" page.
#   * Staging/Production (ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT != Development): the app fail-fasts unless the
#     values below are provided, and Keycloak must be reachable over HTTPS (RequireHttpsMetadata).

# Which environment to run as. Leave as Development for the local Docker stack.
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# --- Database ---
ConnectionStrings__AmcosPostgres=Host=localhost;Database=amcos;Username=postgres;Password=postgr3s;Maximum Pool Size=20;Minimum Pool Size=2

# --- OpenID Connect / Keycloak ---
# These match keycloak/cave-realm.json for the local Docker Keycloak.
OpenIdConnect__Authority=http://localhost:8180/auth/realms/cave
OpenIdConnect__ClientId=amcos-local
OpenIdConnect__ClientSecret=local-dev-secret

# --- URLs / hosts (required when NOT running as Development) ---
AllowedHosts=*
CaveUrl=http://localhost:8180/auth/realms/cave
AmcosUrl=http://localhost:5050/signin-oidc
